00:04:17.709 --> 00:04:20.769
important is the fact
that with Java 7,

00:04:20.769 --> 00:04:22.960
there was a lot of limitations,
among other things,

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:25.540
on security on the ClassLoader.

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:28.330
And that limited the number of
classes that you could load.

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:30.550
So there was that
wide list of classes,

00:04:30.550 --> 00:04:32.680
or Java classes
that were supported.

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:34.450
That has been removed.

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:37.800
And the same thing for the
usual thread execution, which

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:39.520
I wonder how unusual that was.

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:41.120
MARK MANDEL: I wonder
what that means.

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:41.970
There's a story there.

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:43.270
FRANCESC CAMPOY: But
yeah, those two things

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:44.478
have been completely removed.

00:04:44.478 --> 00:04:48.052
So App Engine with Java 8
is basically just Java 8

00:04:48.052 --> 00:04:49.510
