00:28:56.810 --> 00:28:57.907
It's a thing.

00:28:57.907 --> 00:28:58.740
It's quite powerful.

00:28:58.740 --> 00:29:00.980
But maybe I want to pull
data down for backups,

00:29:00.980 --> 00:29:03.320
or I want to put it in BigQuery
or something like that.

00:29:03.320 --> 00:29:05.712
What tools, what things do I
have available to me there?

00:29:05.712 --> 00:29:07.670
FRANCESC CAMPOY: So this
is an interesting one,

00:29:07.670 --> 00:29:10.440
because it's been
changing over the time.

00:29:10.440 --> 00:29:13.850
And at some point-- so
Datastore's beginning was just

00:29:13.850 --> 00:29:15.530
the way you store
data from App Engine.

00:29:15.530 --> 00:29:17.990
It was available
only from App Engine.

00:29:17.990 --> 00:29:20.660
And back then, in
order to do backup

00:29:20.660 --> 00:29:23.360
or to export all of the
data, what you had to do

00:29:23.360 --> 00:29:27.200
was to go into some
console and run MapReduce.

00:29:27.200 --> 00:29:28.700
That would actually
run a MapReduce,

00:29:28.700 --> 00:29:29.660
and you would see the process.

00:29:29.660 --> 00:29:31.610
And you would end up
storing all of this

00:29:31.610 --> 00:29:35.000
into some files in a
Cloud storage bucket.

00:29:35.000 --> 00:29:38.130
Now, the thing is that there
was no API for this at all.

00:29:38.130 --> 00:29:40.310
So you had to go
and do it manually.

00:29:40.310 --> 00:29:45.230
Now, that thing has been
replaced with something

00:29:45.230 --> 00:29:47.469
that we call the Manage
Export and Import Service.

00:29:47.469 --> 00:29:48.760
MARK MANDEL: Ooh, Sounds fancy.

00:29:48.760 --> 00:29:50.218
FRANCESC CAMPOY:
Which, it's fancy,

00:29:50.218 --> 00:29:51.704
but it's beta, just so you know.

00:29:51.704 --> 00:29:52.620
MARK MANDEL: OK, cool.

00:29:52.620 --> 00:29:54.661
FRANCESC CAMPOY: It's an
important thing to know.

00:29:54.661 --> 00:29:56.840
And basically, it allows
you to export and import

00:29:56.840 --> 00:29:59.120
data in a very, very simple way.

00:29:59.120 --> 00:30:01.790
And it's very exciting,
because this time,

00:30:01.790 --> 00:30:04.100
rather than being only
part of the console,

00:30:04.100 --> 00:30:06.160
it's more like what
